WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.780
<i>During their momentary 
holiday, the soccer club</i>

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.170
<i>got into all kinds of trouble,</i>

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.600
<i>but it was a lot of fun.</i>

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>We were all refreshed 
and Seven and Mai-chan</i>

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.570
<i>looked like they had a good time.</i>

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.410
<i>It was a great, fulfilling day.</i>

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.790
<i>But we can't relax forever.</i>

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:25.670
<i>Our next opponent is 
Yoin High, and Asuka-san.</i>

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.640
<i>Today, destiny's whistle will blow.</i>

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Emperor Tooru Asuka</b>

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.280
They're here.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.420
<i>Onimaru-senpai.</i>

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.840
<i>That's Kanagawa's best libero,</i>

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.760
<i>the Emperor, Tooru Asuka.</i>

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.510
I'd like to welcome both 
teams into the stadium.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.370
Let's go!

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.210
Let's go!

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.100
Yeah!

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.380
Good morning, Enoshima.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.650
I'm a little nervous to be 
broadcasting from a real stadium.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.310
I'm known as the "king of commentary,"

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.880
your very own announcer, 
Ichiro Yamanashi.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.460
And never getting a chance to speak,

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:04.530
Momoko Fukushima.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.250
Yamanashi, you talk too much!

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.280
Give her a turn!

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.540
I like you, Momoko!

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.850
Ahem. Now, Fukushima,

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.650
the Yoin High starting 
members, if you would.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:17.280
Okay. I'll now announce the Yoin High

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.260
starting members.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.740
Dad, you're late!

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.530
Mito, Mito...
Just wait a second, Mito.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.440
There goes Mito...

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.210
Over here! Over here!

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.770
Kake-nii is playing in a place like this.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.580
He's like Sugu-nii...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.250
It's time.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.250
I wonder who Saeki-kun 
wants to play against?

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.060
Enoshima, of course. You?

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.270
If I had to choose, Yoin.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.220
I'm more concerned about that guy.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.930
Leonardo Silva?

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.470
I wonder if he has his eye on someone.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.330
With great cheers, both school's eleven

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.860
are heading out to the field.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.800
Asuka-san, look over here!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.610
We love you, Asuka-san!

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.770
We have only moments 
before the semifinals of

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.540
the Kanagawa Inter-high Tournament.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.230
Right now, the captains are on the field

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.130
doing the coin toss.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.520
Yoin!

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.580
Yeah!

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:52.140
Wh-Why is he staring at me?

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.850
Is this really a match we'd come to see?

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.240
We'll find out when the game starts.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:03.250
Playing for Enoshima today are:

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.400
goalkeeper: Akitoshi Ri,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.990
defending: the Horikawa 
and Kaiouji combination,

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.780
defensive middles: first 
year Yakumo on the right,

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:14.820
and Captain Sawamura on the left,

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.790
and the pivotal defensive 
player: Ryoma Oda.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:21.420
On offense, the middle forward:

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.480
the stopper Junpei Hino,

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:26.100
Takase on the left,
 and Matoba on the right.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.970
Below top: Hyodo on the left

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:32.930
and Enoshima's famous fantasista: 
Ryuchi Araki on the right.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.960
It's time for the Yoin match.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.770
Yes.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.860
They've made it this far.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.640
I hope they make it to Nationals.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.480
The ref is about to blow the whistle.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.190
It's the kickoff for 
the semifinals of the

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:54.300
Kanagawa Inter-high Tournament: 
Yoin versus Enoshima.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.090
<i>I see.</i>

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.300
<i>Asuka and Onimaru get all the attention,</i>

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.330
<i>but number 7, Shiratori, 
and number 10, Maya,</i>

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:09.510
<i>are both undoubtedly 
ace players as well.</i>

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.750
<i>Asuka is still on the back line.</i>

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:19.900
<i>As long as he's there, 
even if I create a chance</i>

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.280
<i>he'll shut it down in the end.</i>

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:21.940
Araki-san!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.990
What will Araki do against 
the Yoin defense?

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.570
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:36.150
We only just kicked off, 
but it's so tense.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.100
Even looking from the bench,

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:41.580
I can't see any holes 
in the Yoin defense.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.290
<i>Araki-san.</i>

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.010
If you're going to hold onto 
the ball, I'll come and get it!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.170
Araki-san!

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:49.880
Araki-san.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.290
All right!

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:54.680
Kaoru-kun is open!

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:00.600
Not so fast.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.560
Matoba can't shake him.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.570
He got past him this time.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.300
Amazing! You're amazing, Kaoru-kun!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.780
But he's held on to the 
ball for too long.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:22.730
<i>My feints are working against Yoin.</i>

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.420
Don't get ahead of yourself, first year!

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:29.640
Number 2, Mukai, blocks his path...

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:31.400
Sendo is behind him!

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.890
What will you do, Matoba?

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:34.090
Matoba.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.560
Go!

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:41.680
Matoba's cross goes over Hino's head...

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.730
to Takase!

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.230
It's mine!

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.240
He puts it in with a header!

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.670
We did it!

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:56.550
No!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.960
It's offsides. The offsides flag is up.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:01.950
Crap!

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.620
Too bad, no goal.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.610
Man, we're unlucky.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.150
That's not true, Kota-kun.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:08.800
Huh?

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.080
That was an offsides trap by Yoin.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:15.010
Like a painting, they 
completely drew us in.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.910
Yes, they had set it up

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.850
from the moment of 
Kaoru-kun's penetration.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.190
Kaoru-kun easily slipped past 
Yoin's volante, Sendo-kun,

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:28.070
with a second feint 
and cut to the middle.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.280
In reality, that's what 
they wanted us to do.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.540
Sendo-kun approaches from behind

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.430
and Mukai-kun blocks his path.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:42.250
To avoid it, he kicks an early cross.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.360
Because Hino-kun was already 
in an offsides position,

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.710
Takase gets the ball.

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:52.120
This entire defensive line movement

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.960
was orchestrated by Asuka-kun.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.060
That's...

00:08:57.060 --> 00:09:00.010
I didn't think they would be this good.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:03.480
Their defense is like a pro team's.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.940
We'd better be prepared for some 
difficulty in scoring a goal.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:12.350
Kaoru, cross only after 
bringing the ball in deep.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:13.150
Yes.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.530
<i>I can do it. My dribble 
worked against Yoin.</i>

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:20.150
<i>Next time, I'll push even harder.</i>

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.040
Yoin's volante, Ohtsuki, free kicks to

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.520
below top, number 10, Shinnosuke Maya.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.520
Hyodo, mark Maya.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.500
On it.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:35.970
I won't let you.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:44.810
<i>Kaoru-kun.</i>

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.390
With unmatched athleticism,

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.600
covering from his own 
goal to the front line,

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:55.330
he alone has full reign over 
the field, Tooru Asuka.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.280
You can't leave this player alone.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.420
Huh?

00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.990
Horikawa-kun, he's coming.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:05.220
He kicks it hard towards the front line.

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.300
It's a through pass to Ikusawa.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.130
He saw the movement ahead of him

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.840
and changed to a pass.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.260
No way, no way, no way, no way, no way!

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.220
Katsuragi!

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.180
You...

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:26.860
It's Ri!

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.850
He jumps out and punches.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.560
Heading for the ball is the 
overlapping defender, Asuka.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:36.320
Is he going for a shot?

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.490
I won't let you shoot!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.480
Asuka passes the ball to the right side.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:44.950
The receiver is...

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.660
Onimaru!

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.620
<i>There's no way he can catch that ball.</i>

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.010
He stops the ball! What footwork!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.170
A-Amazing!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.210
Even more amazing is Asuka-san,

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:03.970
who knew to send a pass that 
could just barely be received.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:07.790
<i>You're not getting through!</i>

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.850
Just barely no goal!

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.940
However, the defender Asuka has run all

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.200
the way to the opposing goal.

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.590
This is the true worth of a libero.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.910
What a player...

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:33.840
From his goal to the front line,

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:36.750
even the opposing 
goal is in his territory.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.390
<i>Are you getting excited yet?</i>

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.510
<i>I bet you want to stand 
on the field, Kakeru-kun.</i>

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.120
<i>Am I right?</i>

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:48.140
<i>Suguru, sleeping inside that body, too.</i>

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.270
<i>What about you?</i>

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:05.910
The game restarts with 
Yoin's corner kick.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:07.620
Maya winds up and...

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.500
The defender, Ri, holds onto it.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:14.790
Enoshima has survived one pinch after another,
 now it's time for the counterattack.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.750
Go!

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:21.500
It's a long punt to the 
right side, Matoba.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.430
He's been waiting on the 
front line by himself.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.140
All right. Nice, Kaoru-kun.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.470
Matoba traps the ball with his heel

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:33.890
and from there cuts into the open space.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.670
You're not getting through!

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:36.610
Araki-san!

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:40.770
He's good.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.200
Araki shows his worth 
with a one touch pass.

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:48.340
It's over Maya's head 
to Hyodo behind him.

00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:50.410
Araki comes out on top of 
the number 10 showdown.

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.620
<i>Does he have eyes on 
the back of his head?</i>

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.180
Running around on attack 
against the defense is

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.870
the genius Araki's supporter, Mako-chan.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.040
Originally, he was scouted as a

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.050
below top player for Enoshima's SC.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.500
Be it dribbling, passing, 
or middle shots,

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.560
he's an all-around player 
capable of anything.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:14.560
You're not getting through.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.740
It's Asuka!

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.700
He just attempted a header shot and

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.200
now he's already back 
in front of his goal.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.420
I'd like to request a substitution.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.220
In place of number 7, Matoba,

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.470
number 20, Aizawa, will be going in.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.590
Huh?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.170
They're taking out their 
right wing, Matoba,

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.430
and putting in Aizawa.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.390
Are you ready, Kakeru-kun?

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:58.850
Yes.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.350
Coach!

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.690
Why was I taken out?

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.500
My dribbling was on today, 
and I was creating opportunities.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.820
But you weren't defending at all

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.710
and you didn't return when 
you were supposed to.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:32.130
Against Yoin, I understand 
why you'd be excited,

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:36.340
but in Enoshima's soccer, 
even a forward must defend.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:40.220
Because you were only
 thinking about attacking

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.120
and stayed at the front line,

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.110
Araki-kun was having a 
hard time getting forward

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.070
and you were inviting tight situations.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:48.320
I...

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.230
I'm sorry. I didn't notice.

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:54.180
There's no need to apologize.

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:58.280
There are times when
 that focus on attack

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:00.570
is what leads us to victory.

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:05.590
It's just, Yoin is a team we 
can't give the first goal to.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:06.800
Please understand.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.300
Yes.

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:10.840
That was quick,

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:15.090
but that right wing had to come out.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:16.840
Nice timing.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:19.720
Hola.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:27.710
I see Kakerucchi's just starting.

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.280
Yeah, he starts now.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:31.900
Kakeru-kun.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.320
<i>Kakeru...</i>

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.580
Kake-nii! You can do it!

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:39.440
He's out on the field 20 
minutes into the half,

00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:41.790
the thoroughbred striker, Kakeru Aizawa!

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.190
He's scored five goals
 in the last five games,

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.740
so get that first goal.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:48.960
Break through this standoff!

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.300
<i>Aizawa...</i>

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:57.260
That's Suguru Aizawa's little brother.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.480
Enoshima's ball. 
Sawamura throws in to Oda.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.190
Let's go.

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.650
Araki!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.790
Inaba, number 19.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:08.400
Okay.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.610
On Araki is number 6, Sendo,

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.070
and Onimaru!

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.810
A fast and precise check.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:20.590
Yeah. They were amazing before,

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:21.620
but they're even better now.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:23.080
Araki-san!

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.110
The Enoshima tower, Takase,

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.840
cuts from the left side towards the goal!

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:31.340
No! Asuka-san is bringing up 
the back line again.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:32.550
He'll be offsides.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.760
Araki gets ready to kick.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.550
It's to Aizawa.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:41.590
He suddenly appeared 
near the penalty area.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.980
His first touch has quite the a chance!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:48.630
Using that beanpole as 
bait was a good idea.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.420
That number 10 is watching closely.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:51.690
Here he comes.

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:58.140
But here's Asuka!

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.190
Only Emperor Tooru Asuka 
was paying attention.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:05.830
It's a great mark that's pushing 
Aizawa out of the area.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.600
That number 5 is good.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.850
Suguru's brother will be crushed.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:11.940
I wonder.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.550
You might get to see 
something interesting.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.080
<i>As long as I can't get past Asuka-san,</i>

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.510
<i>I can't pass or shoot. I'll have to...</i>

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:19.730
<i>Come!</i>

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:21.560
There it is!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:33.320
There it is! The Phi Trick!

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.990
Aizawa's finishing feint 
gets him past Asuka!

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:38.870
What was that?

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:41.520
Araki-san!

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:44.040
Aizawa sends it to the center as he falls

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.540
and Araki jumps,

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.500
but he can't reach it.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:52.660
Just watch, I'll show you...

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.160
who's the best!

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.350
Goal!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.640
Ryuichi Araki scores!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:09.610
What a spectacular scorpion shot!

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.570
That was amazing, Araki-san.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.690
Who do you think I am?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.270
More importantly, how does it 
feel to slip past Mr. Emperor?

00:18:19.270 --> 00:18:21.870
Asuka-san was amazing.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.560
I thought I had completely lost him,

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.870
but I was only just able to 
send a low accuracy pass.

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.250
Was that the unpredictability

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.420
you were talking about before?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:36.840
No, I knew about Araki and

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.400
that he was capable of that.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:41.530
I also knew that 
Kakeru Aizawa's feint

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:44.010
couldn't easily be stopped.

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:47.930
Don't worry. I already told you, right?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.330
This is within expectations.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:55.030
Aizawa can only use his feint once.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:58.150
Once you've seen it,
 you can counter it.

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:00.400
I feel better after hearing that.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.180
However, if that was
 within expectations,

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.650
what do you regard as 
unpredictable, Asuka-san?

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:08.050
Who knows?

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:11.210
Because I don't know what it is,

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.580
it's unpredictable.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.470
The game resumes with Yoin's kickoff.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.680
Will the Enoshima Eleven 
harden their defense?

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:23.640
Shiratori!

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:28.700
After Aizawa is Hino, and without 
hardening their defense,

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.310
the Enoshima Eleven take 
an offensive position.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:32.770
I'm counting on you.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.230
I won't let you!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.900
The ball goes to Asuka!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:40.740
You won't get away

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:42.910
with anything but defense!

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:44.990
Here's a fast check.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.830
Araki and Hyodo both attack Asuka.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:49.910
This is good.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:53.680
If Asuka-kun, the libero, 
is commanding from that position,

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:56.620
then the key offensive players, 
Araki-kun and Mako-kun,

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:59.560
should defend with their usual line.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:02.190
That's true. If we can 
steal the ball here,

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:05.850
we can go straight into an attack 
against Asuka-san's defense.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.810
This is a showdown worth watching!

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:10.270
Asuka-san!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.440
Asuka gets ready to kick. 
Could this be...

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:16.890
A long shot?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.400
No way. We're still at the half line.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:25.570
There's a powerful backspin on the ball

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.740
and here's Haruki Onimaru!

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:37.250
Sawamura-kun is doing a great job today.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.960
Really? I feel like they've 
been getting past him.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.610
Onimaru-kun's dribble can't be stopped,

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.380
but by pushing him to the side,

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:48.330
he's applying pressure, 
even when the ball is past him.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:52.120
By making Onimaru-kun's job 
even a little more difficult

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.530
he reduces the risk of losing a goal.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.420
Sawamura-san is running 
around constantly,

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:00.120
but he never loses pace.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.050
Of course.

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:06.010
Sawamura-san's practices 
aren't to be taken lightly.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:14.130
Sawamura-san, you're not done yet?

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:17.630
I'm not like you second 
years who were scouted.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:21.690
What I lack in talent, I have 
to make up for in practice.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:22.590
That's...

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:29.550
Sakamoto, I'll finish any practice, 
no matter how difficult.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:33.110
That way, no matter how fast 
or strong my opponent is,

00:21:33.110 --> 00:21:35.020
I'll never be outrun in the end.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.370
There's no way someone

00:21:38.370 --> 00:21:40.430
like Sawamura-san could lose easily.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:45.030
Damn it!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:48.200
All right.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:49.660
I'm counting on you.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:52.870
Hino is chasing down Oda's pass.

00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>What's Asuka-san doing here?</i>

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:05.020
It's Asuka!

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:07.250
Up until now, he was in 
the midst of the attack,

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:08.900
but he's already back on defense.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.600
What a fast return.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:13.680
I'll use my Phi Trick again...

00:22:15.950 --> 00:22:17.000
Kakeru!

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:20.770
I'll crush you!

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:24.230
Araki slips the ball 
through Ohtsuki's legs.

00:22:26.600 --> 00:22:28.460
He's one-on-one against Asuka.

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:31.330
Will this be a follow-up goal 
or will the Emperor stop him?

00:22:32.390 --> 00:22:34.580
<i>He's aware of where the goalkeeper is</i>

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:37.460
<i>and he's blocking my shot.</i>

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:38.620
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:46.240
It's mine!

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:47.590
It's Aizawa!

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:53.060
Asuka blocks it!

00:22:53.060 --> 00:22:55.060
What unbelievable reaction time.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:22:57.180
What a player.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:59.690
The ball is still in play.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:03.690
This time Inaba blocks it.

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:05.280
Leave it to me!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.860
This is bad. They're countering!

00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:14.790
How far is he taking it?

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:18.040
What's your target?

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:19.040
Ri-san!

00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:23.630
It's Asuka!

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:28.540
He stopped Enoshima's attack 
and now he's overlapping!

00:23:28.540 --> 00:23:30.590
He's running towards the goal!

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:36.390
Just before the end line, 
Onimaru sends a cross...

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:41.100
No, wait. This is...

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:44.520
a shot!

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:58.330
Goal! They've scored.

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:02.810
The ball changed course and 
was sucked into the net.

00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:04.880
Haruki Onimaru is a man to be feared.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:07.820
Y-You're kidding.

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:09.590
That guy...

00:24:10.290 --> 00:24:11.800
Damn it!

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:13.470
Asuka was a distraction.

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:19.440
Attacking the goal from barely 
in front of the end line...

00:24:20.170 --> 00:24:21.830
That was a coincidence, right?

00:24:22.590 --> 00:24:25.860
That shot was no coincidence.

00:24:26.720 --> 00:24:30.770
That's the result of 
endless and tiring practice.

00:24:32.070 --> 00:24:35.980
Amazing. What an amazing team

00:24:35.980 --> 00:24:38.080
Yoin High is.

00:24:45.960 --> 00:25:15.400
<b>Next Episode:
Desperate
 Situation</b>

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:49.600
With Kanagawa's Emperor,
 Tooru Asuka,

00:24:49.600 --> 00:24:51.290
Yoin High continues to rise.

00:24:51.290 --> 00:24:53.220
Demonstrating their
 unstoppable flow,

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:55.440
they clearly show their strength.

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:58.390
Enoshima's attack continues 
to be completely blocked.

00:24:58.390 --> 00:25:00.080
To find the one path 
that will lead Enoshima

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:01.270
to a chance at victory,

00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:03.640
the team attempts 
a new strategy.

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.410
The whole team 
creates the opportunity

00:25:05.410 --> 00:25:08.070
and the ball is 
entrusted to Kakeru.

00:25:08.070 --> 00:25:09.610
Next time on 
Knight in the Area,

00:25:09.610 --> 00:25:12.240
episode 23: "Desperate Situation."

00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:13.740
Everyone worked hard to 
get the ball to you...

00:25:13.740 --> 00:25:15.360
Put it in, Kakeru!
